  "final_response": "- The Git Fusion virtual‑machine image includes a certificate that is issued for a domain name, which does not match the VM’s IP address, so Git will reject the HTTPS connection when cloning or otherwise accessing the repository over HTTPS [client-p4.003-setting-up].  \n- Setting the environment variable `GITSSLNO_VERIFY=true` tells Git not to verify SSL certificates, allowing the HTTPS connection to succeed for testing purposes [environment.006-networking].",
